From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:37:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: let the desktop run while a level loads

RISC OS multitasks cooperatively: other tasks only run when we call
Wimp_Poll, which SDL does from SDL_PumpEvents() in a desktop window.
The game pumps events once per frame of its main loop, but not while a
level loads, so the whole desktop froze on the loading screen (a
campaign load took minutes on a Pi 4). loadingScreenCallback(), which
redraws the progress bar at most every 50ms, now pumps events too.
Events that arrive meanwhile wait in SDL's queue for the main loop.
---
 src/wrappers.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/wrappers.c b/src/wrappers.c
index 425efe0..211abbf 100644
--- a/src/wrappers.c
+++ b/src/wrappers.c
@@ -43,6 +43,10 @@
 #include "warzoneconfig.h"
 #include "wrappers.h"
 
+#if defined(WZ_OS_RISCOS)
+#include <SDL.h>
+#endif
+
 typedef struct _star
 {
 	int      xPos;
@@ -314,6 +318,12 @@ void loadingScreenCallback(void)
 
 	pie_ScreenFlip(CLEAR_OFF_AND_NO_BUFFER_DOWNLOAD);//loading callback		// dont clear.
 	audio_Update();
+#if defined(WZ_OS_RISCOS)
+	// Let the rest of the desktop run: RISC OS multitasks cooperatively,
+	// and in a desktop window SDL_PumpEvents() calls Wimp_Poll. Events
+	// that arrive are queued for the main loop after loading.
+	SDL_PumpEvents();
+#endif
 }
 
 // fill buffers with the static screen
